<h2>Two fuels, two jobs</h2>
<p>Petrol (motor spirit / PMG) powers most cars and almost all motorcycles in Pakistan. High-speed diesel (HSD) powers many pickups, buses, trucks, generators and farm machines. Choosing between them is rarely a lifestyle preference; it is an engine decision made when you buy the vehicle.</p>
<p>Still, households compare which is cheaper every time OGRA revises both. The honest answer is cost per kilometre, not the bigger number on the board.</p>
<p>Fuel Prices PK lists both fuels nationally and by city so you can compare side by side before a trip or a purchase decision.</p>
<h2>Price boards versus cost per km</h2>
<p>Open petrol price today and diesel price today. Note both rupee-per-litre figures, then divide each by your real-world km/L. A diesel that returns 18 km/L can beat a petrol car at 11 km/L even when HSD is a few rupees dearer per litre.</p>
<p>Brochure mileage is optimistic. City congestion, AC load, tyre pressure and roof carriers all matter. The mileage calculator helps you measure tanks honestly after fills.</p>
<p>For a sample intercity route, use the trip cost calculator twice: once with petrol assumptions and once with diesel assumptions at current rates.</p>
<h2>Engines and driving feel</h2>
<p>Petrol spark-ignition engines are quieter at idle and usually cheaper to buy in the passenger segment. Diesel compression-ignition engines deliver strong low-RPM torque suited to loaded highway work.</p>
<p>Stop-go Karachi or Lahore traffic often favours petrol for comfort. Long Multan to Karachi or Peshawar to Islamabad commercial runs still favour diesel economics when loads are heavy.</p>
<p>Maintenance patterns differ too: diesel particulate concerns, injector care and service intervals should factor into total cost of ownership beyond the pump price.</p>
<h2>Policy and product benchmarks</h2>
<p>HSD tracks gasoil-linked international assessments; petrol tracks gasoline-linked ones. Levy and tax treatment can also differ by product over time. That is why a week of oil-down headlines may still produce uneven MS versus HSD moves.</p>
<p>City landings let you open petrol and diesel for the same city side by side, for example Karachi petrol next to Karachi diesel, before you fill for a long drive.</p>
<p>LPG and CNG are separate conversations; do not treat cylinder or CNG kg rates as interchangeable with litre prices without converting energy and vehicle efficiency carefully.</p>
<h2>Practical checklist</h2>
<p>If you already own the vehicle, the fuel is fixed: optimise pressure, service and route planning instead. If you are buying, weigh purchase price, spare parts, expected annual kilometres and today's HSD-petrol spread, then stress-test with a higher fuel price.</p>
<p>Re-check spreads after each OGRA revision. A diesel advantage can shrink or grow within a month under daily pricing.</p>
<p>Read related guides on fuel saving tips and how prices are calculated so the comparison stays grounded in mechanism, not rumour.</p>
